","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":766},{"base":"H2722","lemma":"חֹרֵב","tr":"cho·rev","gloss":"Horeb","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H7281","lemma":"רֶ֫גַע","tr":"re·ga","gloss":"moment","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":32,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The LORD also said to Moses, “I have seen this people, and they are indeed a stiff-necked people.","from":3},{"book":"EXO","chapter":32,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Now leave Me alone, so that My anger may burn against them and consume them. Then I will make you into a great nation.”","from":3},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I have come down to rescue them from the hand of the Egyptians and to bring them up out of that land to a good and spacious land, a land flowing with milk and honey—the home of the Canaanites, Hittites, Amorites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lordappeared to Abram and said, “I will give this land to your offspring.” So Abram built an altar there to the Lord, who had appeared to him.","from":1},{"book":"NUM","chapter":14,"verse":39,"verseEnd":39,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And when Moses relayed these words to all the Israelites, the people mourned bitterly.","from":4},{"book":"NUM","chapter":16,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Separate yourselves from this congregation so that I may consume them in an instant.”","from":5},{"book":"DEU","chapter":9,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Understand, then, that it is not because of your righteousness that the LORD your God is giving you this good land to possess, for you are a stiff-necked people.","from":3},{"book":"DEU","chapter":9,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD also said to me, “I have seen this people, and they are indeed a stiff-necked people.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"7-11":{"people":[{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":4,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"nun-h5126","name":"Nun","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Joshua","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0168","lemma":"אֹ֫הֶל","tr":"o·hel","gloss":"tent","lang":"h","inPassage":11,"uses":345},{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":766},{"base":"H6607","lemma":"פֶּ֫תַח","tr":"pe·tach","gloss":"entrance","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":164},{"base":"H4264","lemma":"מַחֲנֶה","tr":"ma·cha·neh","gloss":"camp","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":215},{"base":"H6051","lemma":"עָנָן","tr":"a·nan","gloss":"cloud","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":87},{"base":"H5982","lemma":"עַמּוּד","tr":"am·mud","gloss":"pillar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":111},{"base":"H1696","lemma":"דָבַר","tr":"da·var","gloss":"to speak: speak","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1142},{"base":"H2351","lemma":"חוּץ","tr":"chuts","gloss":"outside","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":164},{"base":"H4150","lemma":"מוֹעֵד","tr":"mo·ed","gloss":"meeting: time appointed","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":223},{"base":"H5975","lemma":"עָמַד","tr":"a·mad","gloss":"to stand: stand","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":521}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":12,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"I speak with him face to face, clearly and not in riddles; he sees the form of the LORD. Why then were you unafraid to speak against My servant Moses?”","from":11},{"book":"DEU","chapter":34,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"Since that time, no prophet has risen in Israel like Moses, whom the LORD knew face to face—","from":11},{"book":"EXO","chapter":24,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"So Moses set out with Joshua his attendant and went up on the mountain of God.","from":11},{"book":"DEU","chapter":5,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"The LORD spoke with you face to face out of the fire on the mountain.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"So Jacob named the place Peniel, saying, “Indeed, I have seen God face to face, and yet my life was spared.”","from":11},{"book":"JHN","chapter":15,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"You are My friends if you do what I command you.","from":11},{"book":"JHN","chapter":15,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"No longer do I call you servants, for a servant does not understand what his master is doing. But I have called you friends, because everything I have learned from My Father I have made known to you.","from":11},{"book":"ISA","chapter":55,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Seek the LORD while He may be found; call on Him while He is near.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":3}]},"12-17":{"people":[{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":2,"firstVerse":12}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2580","lemma":"חֵן","tr":"chen","gloss":"favor","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":69},{"base":"H3045","lemma":"יָדַע","tr":"ya·da","gloss":"to know","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":945},{"base":"H4672","lemma":"מָצָא","tr":"ma·tsa","gloss":"to find","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":455},{"base":"H5869","lemma":"עַ֫יִן","tr":"a·yin","gloss":"eye","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":887},{"base":"H2088","lemma":"זֶה","tr":"zeh","gloss":"this","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1176},{"base":"H0859","lemma":"אַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"you(m.s.)","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1092},{"base":"H4994","lemma":"נָא","tr":"na","gloss":"please","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":404},{"base":"H6395","lemma":"פָּלָה","tr":"pa·lah","gloss":"be distinguished","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":766},{"base":"H1571","lemma":"גַּם","tr":"gam","gloss":"also","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":769}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":21,"verse":44,"verseEnd":44,"votes":27,"source":"both","text":"And the LORD gave them rest on every side, just as He had sworn to their fathers. None of their enemies could stand against them, for the LORD delivered all their enemies into their hand.","from":14},{"book":"JOS","chapter":1,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":26,"source":"both","text":"No one shall stand against you all the days of your life. As I was with Moses, so will I be with you; I will never leave you nor forsake you.","from":14},{"book":"MAT","chapter":11,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"Come to Me, all you who are weary and burdened, and I will give you rest.","from":14},{"book":"ISA","chapter":63,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"In all their distress, He too was afflicted, and the Angel of His Presence saved them. In His love and compassion He redeemed them; He lifted them up and carried them all the days of old.","from":14},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"Teach me, O LORD, the way of Your statutes, and I will keep them to the end.","from":13},{"book":"JOS","chapter":22,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"And now that the LORD your God has given your brothers rest as He promised them, you may return to your homes in the land that Moses the servant of the LORD gave you across the Jordan.","from":14},{"book":"PSA","chapter":25,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Show me Your ways, O LORD; teach me Your paths.","from":13},{"book":"PSA","chapter":95,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"So I swore on oath in My anger, “They shall never enter My rest.”","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"18-23":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7355","lemma":"רָחַם","tr":"ra·cham","gloss":"to have compassion","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"H5674","lemma":"עָבַר","tr":"a·var","gloss":"to pass","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":556},{"base":"H2603","lemma":"חָנַן","tr":"cha·nan","gloss":"be gracious","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":78},{"base":"H6697","lemma":"צוּר","tr":"tsur","gloss":"Rocks (of Goats)","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":78},{"base":"H3709","lemma":"כַּף","tr":"kaph","gloss":"palm","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":193},{"base":"H3519","lemma":"כָּבוֹד","tr":"ka·vod","gloss":"glory","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":200},{"base":"H5366","lemma":"נְקָרָה","tr":"ne·qa·rah","gloss":"crevice","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H5526","lemma":"סוּךְ","tr":"sukh","gloss":"to fence","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H2898","lemma":"טוּב","tr":"tuv","gloss":"goodness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":32},{"base":"H0268","lemma":"אָחוֹר","tr":"a·chor","gloss":"back","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":41}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ROM","chapter":9,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"For He says to Moses: “I will have mercy on whom I have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I have compassion.”","from":19},{"book":"ROM","chapter":9,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"Therefore God has mercy on whom He wants to have mercy, and He hardens whom He wants to harden.","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"So Jacob named the place Peniel, saying, “Indeed, I have seen God face to face, and yet my life was spared.”","from":20},{"book":"JHN","chapter":1,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"No one has ever seen God, but the one and only Son, who is Himself God and is at the Fatherʼs side, has made Him known.","from":20},{"book":"1TI","chapter":6,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"He alone is immortal and dwells in unapproachable light. No one has ever seen Him, nor can anyone see Him. To Him be honor and eternal dominion! Amen.","from":20},{"book":"ISA","chapter":6,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Then I said: “Woe is me, for I am ruined, because I am a man of unclean lips dwelling among a people of unclean lips; for my eyes have seen the King, the LORD of Hosts.”","from":20},{"book":"JDG","chapter":6,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"When Gideon realized that it was the angel of the LORD, he said, “Oh no, Lord GOD! I have seen the angel of the LORD face to face!”","from":20},{"book":"PSA","chapter":91,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"He who dwells in the shelter of the Most High will abide in the shadow of the Almighty.","from":22}],"notes":[{"id":"exod-9-16-pharaoh","title":"Raised up so that my name might be proclaimed","kind":"quotation"}],"groups":[]}}